ing `od -c` byte dumps: **1050/1050 identical**, covering handcrafted edge cases (multi-sign, `0x10`, `3.7`, `1e5`, leading zeros, tabs/blank-line separators, truncated input, `INT`/`LONG` boundaries) plus ~1000 fuzzed random-integer and random-junk-byte inputs. Exit codes match, and output is byte-identical for raw binary stdin, UTF-8, `/dev/null`, closed stdin, and pipes.\n\nOne note: the rust-analyzer diagnostic you may have seen on line 75 was a stale snapshot captured mid-write — line 75 is just the closing brace of `is_space`, and a `cargo clean` + full rebuild reports no errors or warnings."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":450,"cache_read_input_tokens":27241,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":450,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d97325ad-ed86-41c3-834d-f49e9cb2f6de","uuid":"721965e9-ff02-40ef-91ca-9f71107aa6c4","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:16:15.902Z"}
